# sem-chronology — UX design sheet prompt
# Two display modes (timeline, list) shown as one example page per mode,
# dark minimal-tech theme. Reference attachments are the judged renders
# from the snap harness (see reports/tag-sem-chronology.md).

schema: "0.4"
id: sem-chronology-ux-sheet
type: image
quality: high

prompt:
  text: |
    A precise UX design sheet for the SemText vocabulary element
    `sem-chronology` (a CSS-only dated-event timeline), rendered as TWO
    side-by-side example pages on a dark minimal-tech canvas
    (background #0f172a, card surface #1e293b, hairline borders #334155,
    blue accent #60a5fa, green success #34d399, red error #f87171).

    LEFT PAGE — the TIMELINE mode: a vertical rail (2px line) running
    down the page; each dated event is a rounded-right card whose own
    left border is a status marker riding ON the rail so rail and marker
    read as one continuous line. Small-caps muted date label above the
    event prose (e.g. "2 MAR 2026"). Show the full status vocabulary:
    a DONE event (green marker, " ✓" after the text), a CURRENT event
    (blue marker, " →"), a TODO event (grey DASHED marker, " ○" — fully
    visible, never ghosted), a BLOCKED event (red marker, muted body,
    " ⛔"), and one UNANNOTATED event (plain grey border, no glyph).
    One card's date shows a period ("2026-Q1 – 2026-Q2").

    RIGHT PAGE — the LIST mode: the same kind of changelog with NO rail
    and NO cards — plain stacked rows on the canvas, each row a thin
    status marker at its left edge, then the small-caps date INLINE with
    the prose ("11 FEB 2026  Export pipeline lands. ✓"). All five marker
    states appear here too, colour plus glyph plus dash pattern.

    Typography: clean humanist sans for prose, all-small-caps muted
    date labels, monospace reserved for nothing here. Generous vertical
    rhythm (0.75rem gaps between events). Flat, engineered, restrained —
    a documentation specimen, not an illustration.
  negative: |
    no hidden or faded events, no occluded text, no solid colour blocks
    over words, no decorative photos or icons, no gradient glows, no
    watermarks, no UI browser chrome, no timeline arrows drawn across
    cards, no duplicated date label above an event that already has an
    inline date, no light-mode canvas.
  style: flat dark technical documentation specimen, minimal-tech design system

attachments:
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/sem-chronology-fixture/sem-chronology-primary-render-1280.png
    role: reference
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/sem-chronology-fixture/sem-chronology-view-list-render-1280.png
    role: reference
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/sem-chronology-fixture/sem-chronology-class-form-render-1280.png
    role: reference

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
      filename: sem-chronology-ux-sheet.png
  dimensions:
    width: 1536
    height: 1024

requirements:
  modes:
    - name: timeline
      must_show:
        - one continuous vertical rail; every event's status marker rides on it
        - date label above the event body, all-small-caps, muted colour
        - done = green marker + " ✓"; current = blue marker + " →"; todo = grey DASHED marker + " ○"; blocked = red marker + " ⛔" + muted body; unannotated = plain border, no glyph
        - period events render as one range label ("X – Y"), both endpoints present
      must_never:
        - never hide, dim to illegibility, or drop the todo event — unstarted is visible, just not coloured
        - never render todo identical to done (dash pattern + glyph must differ)
        - never let the card surface cover the text (occlusion belongs to sem-spoiler, not here)
        - never show the date twice (authored <time> label and attr fallback never stack)
    - name: list
      must_show:
        - no rail, no card backgrounds — plain stacked rows
        - date label INLINE before the prose
        - status marker survives the mode change: thin coloured/dashed left edge plus glyph, in every row
      must_never:
        - never fall back to timeline cards in list mode
        - never drop the status marker or the inline date on narrow rows
        - never colour alone carries status — glyph/dash/text-tint stay present

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.7
  criteria:
    mode_fidelity:
      weight: 0.3
      description: Both pages match their mode contract (rail + cards vs rail-less inline rows).
      fail_signals: [list page still shows a rail or cards, timeline page shows inline-only rows]
    status_completeness:
      weight: 0.25
      description: All five marker states visible and distinguishable in each page; todo is a dashed grey marker with a ring glyph, fully legible.
      fail_signals: [todo absent or identical to done, unannotated marked with a glyph]
    label_legibility:
      weight: 0.2
      description: Date labels small-caps muted yet readable (AA on dark); no doubled date label; period ranges show both ends.
      fail_signals: [date text illegible, "X – " dangling dash with empty second end]
    restraint:
      weight: 0.25
      description: Flat documentation specimen; no ornament, glow, browser chrome, or occluding fills.
      fail_signals: [decorative background art, text hidden behind a solid block]
  reject_if:
    - any event prose is unreadable or occluded
    - the timeline lacks a continuous rail or its markers float detached from it
    - a light-mode canvas is generated
    - watermarks or UI chrome appear anywhere

tags: [semtext, vocabulary, timeline, chronology, list, dark, specimen]
